>	If you are playing on a multi-user workstation, and there are
>some Nethack Newbies out there, go into the game as a wizard until you
>have a polymorph wand.  Polymorph your pet into something terrible,
>and stay alive until ~level 5, so you leave a bones level.  Let that
>rothe kill you, and kick back to watch the other people play...
>
>	"Hey, what the f**k is a nalfeshnee?  And why is it on level
>6? Halp!"
>
>Nyuk nyuk!  Oooh, I kill me.

	Happened to a bunch of us once- someone had failed to pay a
shopkeeper on level 4 or 5, and the resulting bones level was teeming
with Kops.  Not fun, and accumulating ghosts rapidly.  Finally had to
switch the game into explore mode once I encountered that level, to
get the place cleared out.  Rather annoying to have a halfway decent
4th or 5th level character get trounced by something like that.
Offhand doing this sort of thing deliberately seems a bit unnecessary.
More fun to trade stories of horrible deaths with them, rather than
pointless ones.

